#### **3. Result for Your Experiment**

> "The Compare It! tool compares two text files and uses different colors to distinguish identical, added, deleted, and modified content. Green indicates source-only text, red indicates target-only text, and blue indicates changed text. Gray virtual lines help align differences, making it easier to analyze changes and document potential evidence of file modification."
